  "full_response": "**Incident Response Report**\n\n---\n\n**Incident Title:** Exposure of Sensitive API Keys in Public GitHub Repository\n\n**Incident Date:** [Incident Start Date]  \n**Incident Duration:** [Start Date] - [End Date]\n\n**Report Date:** [Current Date]  \n**Reporter:** [Your Name], [Your Position]\n\n---\n\n**Executive Summary**\n\nOn [Incident Start Date], it was discovered that sensitive API keys, including those for payment processing, email services, and cloud infrastructure, were inadvertently exposed in a public GitHub repository. Immediate actions were taken to mitigate the exposure and prevent potential misuse. The incident was contained, and all affected credentials have been regenerated and secured.\n\n---\n\n**Incident Details**\n\n**Introduction**\n\nOn [Date], our automated security monitoring system flagged an issue with one of our public GitHub repositories, which contained sensitive credentials. The exposure was identified in the [Repository Name] repository.\n\n**Impact**\n\nThe exposed credentials included:\n- Payment processing API keys\n- Email service API keys\n- Cloud infrastructure API keys\n\nThe potential impact included unauthorized access to payment systems, sensitive email data breaches, and unauthorized use of cloud resources.\n\n**Timeline of Events**\n\n- **[Date and Time]**: Automated security alert triggered.\n- **[Date and Time]**: Initial assessment confirmed the exposure of sensitive keys.\n- **[Date and Time]**: Incident response team assembled.\n- **[Date and Time]**: Public repository access immediately revoked.\n- **[Date and Time]**: Credentials identified and regenerated.\n- **[Date and Time]**: All systems checked for suspicious activity.\n- **[Date and Time]**: Incident classified as managed and resolved.\n\n**Response Actions**\n\n1. **Immediate Containment**\n   - The exposure was contained by revoking public access to the affected GitHub repository.\n   - Affected application access controls were reviewed and updated.\n\n2. **Impact Assessment**\n   - A comprehensive review was conducted to determine which credentials were exposed and the possible extent of unauthorized access.\n\n3. **Recovery**\n   - All exposed API keys were immediately rotated.\n   - Affected systems and services were reviewed to ensure no unauthorized access occurred.\n\n4. **Communication**\n   - Relevant stakeholders, including legal and compliance teams, were informed.\n   - External communication managed in accordance with our incident response plan.\n\n5. **Forensics and Analysis**\n   - Code review conducted to understand the root cause of the exposure.\n   - Recommendations were made to prevent future exposures, including best practices for credential management.\n\n**Lessons",
